From 9251422f5294cbacf8ef196bc633f3135a98eaac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael Rowlinson <mrowlinson@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 03:56:31 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 22/23] fate: add self-contained ac4 mp4 mux/demux roundtrip

Upstream will not take a testless mux/demux pair. New
api-ac4-mp4-roundtrip-test synthesizes its vectors in code, so the
suite needs no uploaded samples: bare raw_ac4_frame packets (the same
minimal version-2 stereo TOC shape as fate-ac4-parser) plus AC40, AC41
and ext-len AC41 Annex G framings with CRCs solved per frame, muxed to
MP4 and demuxed back, asserting dac4 payload byte-exact vs the DSI
golden at both the box level and the demux extradata level, stsz ==
packets == 4, byte-identical payloads, and post-parse 48 kHz stereo
params. Four negatives fail loud: mux without extradata and mux of a
multi-frame packet refuse EINVAL, a file cut inside dac4 and a dac4
box claiming a 2-byte payload both fail open with INVALIDDATA. Wired
as fate-ac4-mp4-roundtrip behind MP4_MUXER + MOV_DEMUXER + AC4_PARSER.

Plus the T3 encoder->decoder audio roundtrip: synth stereo encodes
to raw AC-4 (GEN, no suite samples) and decodes back, pinning
framemd5 (first frame dts/pts 4096 catches the encoder
initial_padding vs decoder skip offset end to end, with DSI in the
loop). Needs A+C in-stack, so it rides the D tip.

Stacks on Series E: appends to the stack tests/fate/ac4.mak
(and extends the fate-ac4 aggregate) instead of creating it.

Signed-off-by: Michael Rowlinson <mrowlinson@gmail.com>
